@startuml 03-activity-diagram
' Activity diagram for checkout, drawn from OrderService.startCheckout and
' PaymentService.pay. Every decision below is a real branch in that code.
'
' The lane is named again after every endif: PlantUML keeps whichever lane the last
' branch left it in, which would otherwise put service work in the customer's column.

title Online Shop — Activity Diagram: checkout and payment

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FDFDFD
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #4A6FA5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #EEF2F7
skinparam ArrowColor #2C4A73

|#F7FAFF|Customer (cli)|
start
:Choose "Checkout";

|#FFFFFF|OrderService|
:Look up the customer;
if (Is the cart empty?) then (yes)
  |Customer (cli)|
  :Show "Cannot place an order
  from an empty cart";
  stop
endif

|Customer (cli)|
:Pick a shipping address;

|OrderService|
if (Does the address belong
to this customer?) then (no)
  |Customer (cli)|
  :Show "Address does not belong
  to this customer";
  stop
endif

|OrderService|
:Check every cart line again;
note right
  Between adding to the cart and
  checking out, a product may have
  been switched off or sold out.
end note

if (Is every product still
on sale and in stock?) then (no)
  |Customer (cli)|
  :Show which product failed
  and how many are left;
  stop
endif

|OrderService|
:Freeze each CartLine into an OrderLine;
:Work out the total from the frozen
prices and the flat shipping fee;
note right
  The amount is never taken from
  the customer (user story 22).
end note
:Take the ordered units off the shelf;
:Empty the cart;
:Save the order as AWAITING_PAYMENT;

|Customer (cli)|
:Choose "Pay for this order";

|#FFFFFF|PaymentService|
if (Is the order still payable?) then (no)
  |Customer (cli)|
  :Show "Order is already PAID
  or CANCELLED";
  stop
endif

|PaymentService|
:Record a Payment attempt as PENDING;

|#F7FAFF|PaymentGateway|
:Authorise the order's exact total;

|#FFFFFF|PaymentService|
if (Did the gateway approve?) then (yes)
  :Mark the attempt SUCCESSFUL
  with the gateway reference;
  :Mark the order PAID;
  |Customer (cli)|
  :Show the payment reference;
  stop
else (no)
  |PaymentService|
  :Mark the attempt FAILED;
  note right
    The order is left payable on
    purpose, which is what lets
    user story 24 retry. The failed
    attempt is kept either way.
  end note
  |Customer (cli)|
  :Show the refusal reason;
  if (Try again?) then (yes)
    |PaymentService|
    :Start a new attempt
    for the same order;
    detach
  else (no)
    |Customer (cli)|
    stop
  endif
endif

@enduml
